From a3570dfa04e2365804aca54707869d7b15164836 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:23:58 +0100
Subject: [RFC PATCH] sparc64: support shared Oberon MSI queues with legacy
 recovery

Initialize an idle Oberon event queue for recoverable endpoints sharing
a bridge. Give each vector a distinct lifetime message ID and accept
function-masked MSI-X allocation unwind without stopping other endpoints.

Stop delivery on queue failure and notify every affected driver outside
controller locks. Retain published queue storage and never reuse message
IDs; exhaustion falls back to legacy interrupts. Configurations enabling
CPU hotplug, kexec or system sleep also retain legacy interrupts.

Signed-off-by: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
---
